# Explanation why the column 'locCodeAndComment' is dropped
# 'locCodeAndComment' seems redundant because 'lOCode', 'lOComment', and 'lOBlank' provide more granular information about lines of code, comments, and blank lines. The newly created feature 'comment_to_code_ratio' further captures this relationship. Thus, this column is likely unnecessary.
df.drop(columns=['locCodeAndComment'], inplace=True)

# Explanation why the column 'lOComment' is dropped
# The 'lOComment' feature is indirectly included in the new feature 'comment_to_code_ratio'. Retaining it may create multicollinearity and redundancy. Thus, it can be dropped after ensuring no critical information is lost.
df.drop(columns=['lOComment'], inplace=True)

# Explanation why the column 'l' is dropped
# The 'program length (l)' feature overlaps conceptually with 'e' (effort) and the newly created 'normalized_effort' captures the relationship between lines of code and effort more accurately. Thus, it may no longer add additional value to the model.
df.drop(columns=['l'], inplace=True)
