# Similarly, 'b' can be dropped due to having extremely low variance and likely less contribution to the predictive power.
# Explanation why the column 'b' is dropped: The b metric (usually associated with Halstead errors) has a mean of 0.0858 and is not well-distributed.
df.drop(columns=['b'], inplace=True)
end 

